    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Pakistan's elderly population is forecast to triple to over 43 million people over the next three decades, according to the United Nations Population Fund. By 2050, those over the age of 60 are estimated to account for one in six people in the country, a demographic change which has wide-ranging implications for the nursing and healthcare sector.",
